  "summary": "Ask what someone did, answer in the past, and say what you didn't do with مَا.",
  "intro": "To ask 'What did you do?' use مَاذَا + a past verb: مَاذَا فَعَلْتَ؟ (to a man), مَاذَا فَعَلْتِ؟ (to a woman). To say you didn't do something, put مَا in front of the past verb: مَا سَبَحْتُ (I didn't swim). Careful: مَاذَا asks 'what?', but مَا right before a past verb means 'not'.",
  "objectives": [
    "Ask مَاذَا فَعَلْتَ؟ and مَاذَا فَعَلْتِ؟ and answer in the past",
    "Say what you didn't do with مَا + past verb",
    "Use six new holiday verbs: visited, walked, swam, drank, photographed, did",
    "Glide ay and aw in words like شَيْء and يَوْم"
